BT 1 0 0 1 0 50 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 1.550215 Tw (A function is a piece of code that is encapsulated and available for call, generally used to implement a specific) Tj T* 0 Tw .070256 Tw (function. Function is actually a big category, which includes several subtypes such as closures, native functions, and) Tj T* 0 Tw .555783 Tw (native closures. For Berry code, all function subtypes have the same behavior. Functions belong to the first type of) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.472205 Tw (value in Berry, so they can be passed as values. In addition, it can be directly used in expressions through the) Tj T* 0 Tw (\223literal\224 form of \223anonymous functions\224.) Tj T* ET
