BT 1 0 0 1 0 86 Tm .000742 Tw 12 TL /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (After the program executes to the ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (raise) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( statement, it will not continue to execute the statements following it, but will) Tj T* 0 Tw .770783 Tw (jump to the nearest exception handling block. If the most recent exception handling block is in other functions, the) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.026295 Tw (functions along the call chain will exit early. If there is no exception handling block, ) Tj /F2 10 Tf (Abnormal exit) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( will occur, and the) Tj T* 0 Tw .4273 Tw (interpreter will print the exception error message and the call stack of the error location.When the ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (raise) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( statement) Tj T* 0 Tw .174004 Tw (is in the ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (try) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( statement block, the exception will be caught by the latter. The caught exception will be handled by the) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.483005 Tw /F3 10 Tf (except) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( block associated with the ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (try) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( block. If the thrown exception can be handled by the ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (except) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( block, the) Tj T* 0 Tw .199672 Tw (execution of this block will continue from the statement after the last ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (except) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( block. If all ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (except) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( statements cannot) Tj T* 0 Tw (handle the exception, the exception will be rethrown until it can be handled or the exception exits.) Tj T* ET
