BT 1 0 0 1 0 38 Tm .022705 Tw 12 TL /F1 10 Tf 0 0 0 rg (When an exception is caught in the ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (try) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( statement block, the interpreter will check the ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (except) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( branch one by one. If) Tj T* 0 Tw .049277 Tw (the exception value exists in the capture list of a branch, the code block under the branch will be called to handle the) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.264358 Tw (exception, and the entire ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (try-except) Tj /F1 10 Tf ( statement will exit after the code block is executed. If all the ) Tj /F3 10 Tf (except) Tj /F1 10 Tf  T* 0 Tw (branches do not match, the exception will be re-thrown and caught and handled by the outer exception handler.) Tj T* ET
