BT 1 0 0 1 0 50 Tm /F1 10 Tf 12 TL .352321 Tw (Berry\222s class does not support access restrictions, and all properties of the class are visible to the outside. In native) Tj T* 0 Tw .296005 Tw (classes, you can use some tricks to make properties invisible to Berry code \(usually let the member name start with) Tj T* 0 Tw .528205 Tw (dot \223.\224\). You can use some conventions to restrict access to the members of the class, such as the convention that) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.993182 Tw (the attributes starting with an underscore are private attributes. This convention does not have any use at the) Tj T* 0 Tw (grammatical level, but is conducive to the logical structure of the code.) Tj T* ET
